0006: one INT compat type for B8G8R8A8 in the UBWC compat table.

**Status:** shipped in `27.0.0-devel-p14`. Upstream: not sent separately - one of
the ADR-0003 family (0005, 0006, 0010, and the tiling axis of 0014).
**Found:** a list containing B8G8R8A8 lost UBWC because the table had
no INT compat type that its integer views could share.

## For users of other drivers

Nothing to set. A BGRA8 texture whose list also names an integer view keeps
compression instead of losing it, i.e. bandwidth.

## Summary

`FD6_UBWC_B8G8R8A8_INT` is added to the compat switch of `freedreno_ubwc.h`, so
the integer interpretation of a BGRA8 image shares one compat class with the
float one instead of answering `UNKNOWN` and clearing `ubwc_enabled` for the whole
list.

## Evidence

Two hunks in `src/freedreno/common/freedreno_ubwc.h` (the enum row and the
switch). Verified by probe `T` of `tests/rp6-vkd3d-sparse-test.c`: the mutable
list's `memreq` goes `0x100000 -> 0x102000`, i.e. the metadata plane appears
(`docs/artifacts.md` row 0006; journal 16).

## Tests

| what the hunk changes | how it is checked | result |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| a BGRA8 list keeps UBWC | probe `T` memreq, journal 16 | `0x100000 -> 0x102000` |
| probes `S` and `T` still pass | the same run, journals 16 and 20.5 | PASS |
| nothing else moves | the 94-row matrix, journal 24.3 | 94 EXACT |

## The change in this repo

One row, one case; it must not claim compression for a format the layout tables
do not tile. Revert: `git apply -R` with the file name explicit.

## Related

`0011`, `0012` (other rows of the same switch); `0005`, `0010` (tiling side);
ADR-0003.

